report=OUT/'PlanB_related_work_and_novelty_check_20261118.md'
lines=['# Plan B related-work and novelty check','','Date: 2026-11-18','','## Search scope','', '- Primary source: PubMed E-utilities.', '- Lateral source: OpenAlex.', '- PubMed searches used five complementary query sets covering HF integrative studies, cardiotoxicity single-cell studies, HF fibrosis/cytotoxic programmes, doxorubicin single-cell studies, and ICI myocarditis single-cell/spatial studies.', '- PubMed returned 40 records per query and 183 unique records after deduplication across the five query sets.', '- This is a targeted novelty check, not an exhaustive systematic review. Web of Science, Scopus, Embase, and CNKI were not searched in this pass.', '', '## Bottom line','', 'Similar papers exist and are numerous, but no published paper with the exact same combination was found in this search. The exact combination is:', '', '> cross-dataset harmonized single-cell/single-nucleus/spatial module scoring across human HF, human DoxCM/NICM and mouse ICI cardiotoxicity, with explicit DoxCM-versus-NICM comparison and a reproducible directional synthesis.', '', 'The novelty is therefore **integrative and methodological**, not the first discovery of fibrosis, cytotoxic T cells, DoxCM biology, or the ICI immune niche.', '', '## Closest related articles','', '| Category | Paper | Year | Why it matters | Our differentiation |','|---|---|---:|---|---|']
for r in rows:
    cat,first,year,journal,title,pmid,doi,what,relation=r
    lines.append(f'| {cat} | {first}, {journal}; PMID {pmid}; DOI {doi}. **{title}** | {year} | {what} | {relation} |')
lines += ['', '## Strongest overlap by dimension','', '### 1. Same dataset / direct predecessor','', '- **Guo et al., Circulation 2025 (GSE292067)** is the closest direct predecessor. It already compares DoxCM, NICM and donors and validates CD47. Our manuscript must clearly state that GSE292067 is a public source dataset and that our contribution is the cross-dataset programme comparison, not the discovery of DoxCM or CD47.', '- **Youness et al., Genome Medicine 2025 (GSE298023)** already dissects fibroblast activation and spatial heterogeneity. Our fibroblast fibrosis finding must be positioned as consistency across datasets, not a new fibroblast subtype discovery.', '- **Pan et al., Circulation 2025 (GSE288222)** is the source isoform atlas. Our gene-level module score is not a replacement for isoform-level analysis.', '', '### 2. Human HF spatial landscape','', '- **Lee et al., European Heart Journal 2025** is the closest human HF spatial study. It uses GeoMx in 90 cores from 44 participants and links endothelial inflammatory states to fibrosis. Our spatial evidence is from mouse ICI Visium and should not be described as a new human spatial atlas.', '', '### 3. Cross-dataset methodology','', '- **Huang et al., Briefings in Bioinformatics 2026** is the closest cross-dataset computational paper, but it focuses on HCM and an ENPP2+ macrophage-fibroblast axis, with experimental validation. Our study differs by comparing HF and cancer therapy-related cardiotoxicity and by using a harmonized module-score framework.', '- **Li et al., Cardiovascular Research 2023** establishes a multi-species single-cell meta-analysis precedent, but focuses on endothelial responses after ischemic injury.', '', '### 4. Doxorubicin cytotoxic-T mechanism','', '- **Bayer et al., Nature Cardiovascular Research 2024** provides direct functional evidence that CD8+ cytotoxic T cells drive doxorubicin-induced fibrosis and systolic dysfunction. This strongly supports our directional finding but also means we cannot claim the cytotoxic-T/fibrosis mechanism as our discovery.', '', '### 5. ICI myocarditis immune/spatial niche','', '- **Blum et al., Nature 2024** shows co-localization of cytotoxic T cells, dendritic cells and inflammatory fibroblasts in human ICI myocarditis.', '- **Sun et al., Journal of Translational Medicine 2025** highlights CXCL9+ fibroblasts and ACKR1+ endothelial cells in immune-related myocarditis.', '- **Zhu et al., Circulation 2022** and **Ma et al., Circulation 2024** establish cytotoxic CD8+ T cells and pathogenic macrophages in ICI myocarditis.', '- These papers are more granular and mechanistically deeper than our module-level synthesis. Our claim should remain at the level of cross-dataset programme convergence.', '', '## What is genuinely new in our paper','', '1. A single harmonized module-scoring framework applied across seven HF/cardiotoxicity datasets and multiple platforms.', '2. An explicit DoxCM-versus-NICM comparison showing substantial programme overlap and lack of an FDR-significant chemotherapy-exclusive signature.', '3. A cross-dataset directional synthesis of Fibrosis-ECM and Cytotoxic-T programmes across human HF and cancer therapy-related cardiotoxicity.', '4. A reproducible clean-room analysis package with file-level and figure-level QA.', '', '## What is not new and must not be claimed','', '- First discovery of human DoxCM single-cell biology.', '- First discovery of CD47, POSTN+ fibroblasts, cytotoxic T cells or macrophage subsets.', '- First human HF spatial atlas.', '- First ICI myocarditis immune atlas.', '- Causal proof that fibrosis or cytotoxic T cells drive disease.', '- Evidence that any TCM intervention works.', '', '## Reviewer risk','', 'The main reviewer objection will be: **“What does this add beyond reanalysis of already published datasets?”**', '', 'The defensible answer is:', '> We do not claim new biology. We provide a harmonized cross-dataset comparison that distinguishes recurrent directional programmes from dataset-specific findings, documents the DoxCM/NICM overlap, and supplies a reproducible evidence map for hypothesis generation.', '', '## Recommended Frontiers positioning','', 'Use a title and abstract that emphasize **cross-dataset exploratory synthesis**, not target discovery. Avoid “identifies a therapeutic target” and avoid “first” claims. A suitable framing is:', '', '> Cross-dataset single-cell and spatial transcriptomic analysis of recurrent fibrotic and cytotoxic T-cell programmes in heart failure and cancer therapy-related cardiotoxicity.', '', '## Files','', f'- Curated article table: `{csv_path}`', '- PubMed raw search export: `PlanB_related_literature_pubmed_20261118.csv`']
report.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
